  "summary": {
    "en": {
      "caveats": null,
      "what": "The authors developed Conditional Diffusion-based Parameter Generation (CDPG), a framework that generates node-specific predictor parameters for data-scarce target cities instead of aligning raw data from data-rich source cities. The approach guides parameter generation using base station-level spatio-temporal contexts, combining satellite imagery with LLM-derived semantic summaries for spatial features and unsupervised pattern clustering for temporal dynamics. Evaluated on three large-scale traffic datasets, CDPG improved forecasting accuracy over state-of-the-art few-shot cross-city baselines by up to 9.72%.",
      "why": "This approach shifts cross-city transfer learning from brittle data-space alignment to model-parameter generation, enabling reliable mobile traffic forecasting in newly deployed or under-instrumented urban regions."
    }
